    "title": "How to watch Open Championship for free: TV channels, streaming info - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The 153rd edition of the Open Championship is here and Northern Ireland's Royal Portrush Golf Club is set to host the world's best golfers for the final major tournament of the 2025 season. Scottie Scheffler and Rory McIlroy are the pre-event betting favorites and American Xander Schauffele is back as the defending champion . But links courses involves strategy and precision the traditional PGA Tour set up doesn't and often adds to the intrigue and drama with an international field that also features guaranteed slots for the DP World Tour and LIV Golf . First-round action got underway on Thursday, July 17 across the pond with the first tee times in the wee hours of the morning stateside. Here's a look at how to watch the 2025 Open Championship for free, including TV channels and live streaming options for each day of the tournament: OPEN CHAMPIONSHIP PREDICTIONS: AI picks best bets, sleepers based on 2025 odds The 153rd edition of the Open Championship is scheduled to begin with first-round action on Thursday, July 17 and continues through the final round scheduled for Sunday, July 20, at Royal Portrush Golf Club in County Antrim, Northern Ireland. Live coverage of this year's Open Championship will be provided by NBC, USA Network, Golf Channel and Peacock . Live streaming is also available via Fubo , which is offering a free trial for new subscribers. All times Eastern Rounds 1 and 2 Round 4 Watch the British Open with Fubo Fans can stream select coverage through the NBC Sports App, and can catch the entire tournament on Fubo , which currently offers a free trial subscription for new users. This article originally appeared on USA TODAY: How to watch Open Championship for free: TV channels, streaming info",
